+++ b/docs/memory/decision-log/dl-005-generate-structural-json-patch-diffs.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+---
+id: dl-005-generate-structural-json-patch-diffs
+type: decision-log
+title: "Generate structural JSON Patch diffs"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Clients need to transmit concise RFC 6902 updates rather than whole JSON documents. Replacing a
+changed parent object or array would unnecessarily resend unrelated values.
+
+## Decision
+
+Generate patches recursively for objects and use escaped RFC 6901 pointer paths. For arrays, choose
+a deterministic minimum edit sequence of additions, removals, and aligned replacements; recurse
+into aligned replacements so a changed member of an array object remains a member-level operation.
+Validate both inputs as JSON values and clone values inserted into the returned patch.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Small nested edits produce correspondingly small patches, while array insertion and removal retain
+unaffected elements. Patch generation uses quadratic time and memory in array lengths to select its
+edit sequence.
